commit 0b1d4a2eeb25e5df0e8557a2ac38a12dbb3d99bb
Author: Makapania <matt.sponheimer@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat May 2 14:38:53 2026 -0600

    feat(T-19): add Auto mode — detect imbalance, apply class_weight if ≥3:1
    
    The user's framing memo (project_t19_user_framing.md) called for either
    per-model UI dropdowns OR an auto-detect mode. Per-model dropdowns are
    deferrable; Auto mode is the priority — without it, T-19 isn't done.
    
    What ships:
    
    - New `'auto'` option in the GUI imbalance dropdown (9th option, bottom of
      the classification list). Tooltip explains the 3:1 trigger.
    - New helper `imbalance.resolve_auto_imbalance(y, task_type, threshold=3.0)`
      returns ('class_weight', info) on imbalanced data, (None, info) on
      balanced data, (None, {}) for regression. Single source of truth.
    - Runtime resolution at the entry of `run_search` (search.py), `run_nsga2_search`
      (nsga2_search.py), and `run_unified_bayesian` (unified_bayesian.py): when
      `imbalance_method='auto'`, mutate to either 'class_weight' or None based
      on the global y's class ratio. Print the audit line either way.
    - Code generator emits a runtime-resolution block at the end of the imbalance
      handling section. Generated scripts mutate IMBALANCE_METHOD post-load so
      the existing class_weight gates fire correctly without needing to know
      about 'auto'. Per-library kwargs (auto_class_weights for CatBoost, sample_weight
      for XGBoost via fit_kwargs) are baked at codegen time as if 'auto' were
      'class_weight'; on balanced data the runtime resolution prevents the
      sample_weight block from firing and the baked class_weight='balanced' is a
      mathematical no-op (uniform per-class weights).
    - `validate_classification_config` accepts 'auto' the same as 'class_weight'
      (no resampling-specific validation needed).
    
    Tests:
    - 17 new tests in `test_t19_auto_mode.py`: resolver contract (imbalanced ratio,
      balanced ratio, regression task, custom threshold), codegen emission per
      library (CatBoost auto_class_weights, XGBoost sample_weight, RF/LightGBM
      class_weight, MLP no-injection), end-to-end exec on imbalanced AND balanced
      synthetic data.
    - 18 existing class_weight tests still green.
    - 336 passed + 2 skipped on the consolidated regression sweep including
      imbalance suite.
    
    Per-model UI dropdowns (separate `is_unbalance` / `scale_pos_weight` /
    `auto_class_weights` selectors) remain deferred — explicit user direction
    that those add UI surface without statistical-equivalence improvement.

